{"name":"Winterkeep","status":"ok","title":"Winterkeep","pageId":10787,"html":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"mw-empty-elt\">\n</p><aside role=\"region\" class=\"portable-infobox pi-background pi-border-color pi-theme-frwiki pi-layout-default type-location\">\n\n\n<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-item-spacing pi-title pi-secondary-background\" data-source=\"name\">Winterkeep</h2>\n<section class=\"pi-item pi-group pi-border-color\">\n\t<h2 class=\"pi-item pi-header pi-secondary-font pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-background\">Geography</h2>\n\n<div class=\"pi-item pi-data pi-item-spacing pi-border-color\" data-source=\"region\">\n\t\n\t\t<h3 class=\"pi-data-label pi-secondary-font\">Region</h3>\n\t\n\t<div class=\"pi-data-value pi-font\">the <a href=\"/wiki/Hordelands\" title=\"Hordelands\">Hordelands</a>, <a href=\"/wiki/Northeast_Faer%C3%BBn\" title=\"Northeast Faerûn\">northeast Faerûn</a></div>\n</div>\n\n</section>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Inhabitants_of_Winterkeep\" title=\"Category:Inhabitants of Winterkeep\">Inhabitants of  Winterkeep</a></nav>\n<nav class=\"pi-navigation pi-item-spacing pi-secondary-font\"><a href=\"/wiki/Category:Organizations_in_Winterkeep\" title=\"Category:Organizations in Winterkeep\">Organizations in  Winterkeep</a></nav>\n</aside>\n\n<p class=\"mw-empty-elt\"></p><p><b>Winterkeep</b> was a ruin located on the southern tip of the <a href=\"/wiki/Yal_Tengri\" title=\"Yal Tengri\">Yal Tengri</a>. East of Winterkeep were the <a href=\"/wiki/Glittering_Spires\" title=\"Glittering Spires\">Glittering Spires</a>. \n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Description\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Description</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#History\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">History</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Appendix\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Appendix</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#References\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">References</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Description\">Description</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Description\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&section=1\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Description\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>On the surface, only rubble remained, but the extensive subterranean passageways and chambers remained mostly intact. The royal family and their servants retreated beneath the surface during winter storms; as a result these halls were comfortably furnished.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p108-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>To the <a href=\"/wiki/Vil_Adanrath\" title=\"Vil Adanrath\">Vil Adanrath</a>, Winterkeep was known as \"<i>Iket Sotha</i>\".<sup id=\"cite_ref-FF-p60_2-0\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-FF-p60-2\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"History\">History</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: History\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&section=2\" aria-label=\"Edit section: History\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Winterkeep was built as a nobleman's estate, in the days of <a href=\"/wiki/Raumathar\" title=\"Raumathar\">Raumathar</a>. It later became a retreat for the royal family. After the fall of the empire, Winterkeep gradually fell to ruins.<sup id=\"cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-1\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-TH.VII-p108-1\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p><p>In <a href=\"/wiki/1374_DR\" title=\"1374 DR\">1374 DR</a>, the <a href=\"/wiki/Gelugon\" title=\"Gelugon\">gelugon</a> <span class=\"new\" title=\"Ultael (page does not exist)\" data-uncrawlable-url=\"L3dpa2kvVWx0YWVsP2FjdGlvbj1lZGl0JnJlZGxpbms9MQ==\">Ultael</span> enslaved several <a href=\"/wiki/Ice_troll\" title=\"Ice troll\">ice troll</a> warbands and started to attempt to make a fiefdom for himself. He sent several warbands out to raid along the <a href=\"/wiki/Golden_Way\" title=\"Golden Way\">Golden Way</a>.<sup id=\"cite_ref-3\" class=\"reference\"><a href=\"#cite_note-3\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\">]</span></a></sup>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Appendix\">Appendix</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: Appendix\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&section=3\" aria-label=\"Edit section: Appendix\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"References\">References</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a title=\"Edit section: References\" class=\"mw-editsection-visualeditor\" data-tracking-label=\"edit-section-anon\" data-action=\"edit-section\" href=\"https://forgottenrealms.fandom.com/wiki/Winterkeep?veaction=edit&section=4\" aria-label=\"Edit section: References\"></a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<div class=\"reflist\">\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap\"><ol class=\"references\">\n<li id=\"cite_note-TH.VII-p108-1\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\">↑ <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-0\">1.0</a></sup> <sup><a href=\"#cite_ref-TH.VII-p108_1-1\">1.1</a></sup></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/David_Cook\" title=\"David Cook\">David Cook</a>&#160;(August 1990). “Volume II”. In <a href=\"/wiki/Steve_Winter\" title=\"Steve Winter\">Steve Winter</a>&#160;ed. <i><a href=\"/wiki/The_Horde\" title=\"The Horde\">The Horde</a></i> (<a href=\"/wiki/TSR,_Inc.\" title=\"TSR, Inc.\">TSR, Inc.</a>), p. 108. ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-88038-868-4\">0-88038-868-4</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-FF-p60-2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-FF-p60_2-0\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Mark_Sehestedt\" title=\"Mark Sehestedt\">Mark Sehestedt</a>&#160;(2006). <i><a href=\"/wiki/Frostfell\" title=\"Frostfell\">Frostfell</a></i>. (<a href=\"/wiki/Wizards_of_the_Coast\" title=\"Wizards of the Coast\">Wizards of the Coast</a>), p. 60. ISBN&#160;<a href=\"/wiki/Special:BookSources/0-7869-4245-2\" title=\"Special:BookSources/0-7869-4245-2\">0-7869-4245-2</a>.</span>\n</li>\n<li id=\"cite_note-3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-3\">↑</a></span> <span class=\"reference-text\"><a href=\"/wiki/Edward_Bonny\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Edward Bonny\">Edward Bonny<